1
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,037
YAMU!

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:12,797
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,960
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,620
You're on the move!

5
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,934
Seems like the pharaoh's in
pretty bad shape down there.

6
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,000
Of course.

7
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,129
There's still a hole in his
heart that has yet to be filled.

8
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:16,860
Poor guy.

9
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:20,181
He still blames himself
for what happened to Yugi.

10
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:23,670
Yugi.

11
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,400
If it weren't for me, you'd still be here.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,557
i'll never forgive myself

13
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:37,040
time for you to pay up pharaoh

14
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:46,497
no yuki stop what are
you doing here it only

15
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:49,580
needs one of us so i'm
letting the seal take me

16
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:02,397
instead. No. Yugi.

17
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,920
Mark my words.

18
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,357
I won't rest until I get you back.

19
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,780
It's not fair.

20
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,110
I should

21
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,442
be locked away.

22
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,620
Not you.

23
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,477
I'm the one who played that evil card.

24
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,417
He's got to snap out of this.

25
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:21,040
If he keeps wallowing in the
past, we'll never find Yugi.

26
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,380
Hang in there.

27
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,900
Well, what do you know?

28
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:35,160
The pharaoh did survive, but
I'm gonna have to change that.

29
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:59,980
This had better be good I've
located the Feral Master Nice work,

30
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:03,880
for once Now all I have to
do is finish what I started

31
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,540
No, you fool

32
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,780
Something's got me, sir
How observant of you

33
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,957
That valley is inhabited
by evil apparitions,

34
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:23,340
but I would never expect your
minuscule brain to comprehend that.

35
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,778
Now throw your stone into the ruins.

36
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,240
Ancient spirits of the Orychalcos,

37
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,217
I call humbly upon thee
to awaken the soul of

38
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,947
one of your own from
the depths of the earth.

39
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:45,400
Come forth, my Orychalcos soldier,
and bring the pharaoh to me.

40
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,800
What's this?

41
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,198
It's an earthquake!

42
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,540
Oh, no!

43
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,320
I'm afraid it's worse than that.

44
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:03,900
Show yourself!

45
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,740
I thought so.

46
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:31,400
Who are you?

47
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,148
And what is this all about?

48
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:38,360
Not much of a talker, I
see. Careful, Pharaoh.

49
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:41,366
This creature is more
dangerous than you know.

50
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,165
You've seen this thing before?

51
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:51,140
I hope it's on my side Welcome back,

52
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:57,780
my child It's time to wage war
again And this time We'll win

53
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:12,700
Close your eyes and see the truth Spirits
What is it you're trying to show me?

54
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,000
The past

55
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:17,537
I see something...

56
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:19,400
Evil soldiers!

57
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,320
Hold on!

58
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,140
The ancient war!

59
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:27,300
The one Raphael told me about!

60
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:32,000
The world was divided into two sides.

61
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:35,120
The pure of heart and
those ruled by darkness.

62
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:40,780
The two sides faced off in the most
devastating battle the world's ever seen.

63
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:46,260
An army of duel monsters fought
the soldiers of the Orichalcos?

64
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,618
Could that be how the city
of Atlantis was destroyed?

65
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:55,255
But what does this ancient battle
have to do with what's going on today?

66
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:57,250
Wait!

67
00:05:57,333 --> 00:05:59,438
That looks like Chris and Ironheart!

68
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,100
But how can that be?

69
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:10,480
what does this mean

70
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:18,017
i once fought this very
soldier and his army in the

71
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:22,137
great battle to save
atlantis did you say atlantis

72
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:25,697
this is the same spot where
we made our last stand

73
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:29,760
against the evil lord darts
and now the battle continues

74
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,780
Now, my Orychalcos soldier,

75
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:39,537
harness the power of the very
source from which you were born,

76
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:42,760
and conjure the ancient
seal of Orychalcos!

77
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,380
Oh, no!

78
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,520
This is bad!

79
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:56,337
Looks like his fate is sealed.

80
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:57,960
Nice known ya, pharaoh!

81
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,840
Be careful!

82
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:08,680
What do you want?

83
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,580
He wants to duel.

84
00:07:14,380 --> 00:07:16,520
Did he just summon a monster?

85
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:28,300
Meet Orychalcos Gygas!

86
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,040
Attack the Pharaoh!

87
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:44,280
Fear not, my Pharaoh.

88
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:53,407
The lost spirits of Atlantis are
here to protect you, Pharaoh.

89
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:56,300
But they cannot act alone.

90
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:59,796
Summon your monsters and the
spirits will assist them.

91
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,261
Very well, then.

92
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:08,760
Together, we'll take down this beast.

93
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:17,860
I summon Gazelle, the king of
mythical beasts, and Berfomet!

94
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:26,300
Now I play Polymerization, fusing
my monsters to form Chimera,

95
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,069
the flying mythical beast!

96
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:30,400
Attack, Chimera!

97
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:51,360
It's back, but now it has
even more attack points.

98
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:54,420
Go, Chimera!

99
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:12,960
Every time I attack his monster,
it comes back even stronger.

100
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:16,020
My fissure magic card should stop it.

101
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:20,420
It worked!

102
00:09:23,660 --> 00:09:25,480
Or, maybe not.

103
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:28,720
It must be immune to magic cards.

104
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:38,040
When Chimera is destroyed,
my gazelle returns!

105
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,260
Not so fast!

106
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:44,857
I play my Mirror Force Trap card!

107
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:47,560
It reflects your attack right back!

108
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,760
Here we go again.

109
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:58,260
Traps don't work either.

110
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,280
Nothing can stop it.

111
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:07,040
But I must protect my life points.

112
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,140
Go, obnoxious Celtic Guardian!

113
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,140
Are you all right?

114
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,020
Look out!

115
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,620
One more attack, and I'm finished.

116
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:39,760
I've got you right where
I want to, Phantom.

117
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:52,617
Let's see you get yourself
out of this He's about to lose

118
00:10:52,700 --> 00:10:57,060
There is but one thing that can
save him The card he gave you?

119
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:02,120
The Eye of Tumaius

120
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:06,160
The creature that fought
by my side so long ago

121
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:09,410
Grandpa!

122
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:17,160
Tumaius' old friend Please bring
peace to our land once again.

123
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:21,460
That vision, it's happening again.

124
00:11:21,880 --> 00:11:24,380
I can see the ancient battle of Atlantis.

125
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:34,000
You there, run!

126
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,820
You're outnumbered!

127
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,420
Ironheart, no!

128
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:47,020
It's Chris!

129
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,360
Nice shot!

130
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,226
But you still need more help!

131
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:56,420
It's Tomaeus!

132
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:20,980
Who is that?

133
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:29,180
Don't be a fool, Timaeus.

134
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:31,820
You can't stop me.

135
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:36,640
I hold more power in my finger
than you do in your whole body.

136
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:52,500
You don't know when to quit

137
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:56,660
Arm to me, sword of kings

138
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:11,980
No, to my ass

139
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:18,510
Farewell.

140
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:21,600
Great Leviathan, finish him off!

141
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:52,585
He'll never fight off
those evil spirits alone.

142
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:53,760
Come on, Skye.

143
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:56,660
Chris, wait!

144
00:13:57,480 --> 00:14:00,420
I must protect the Pharaoh or all is lost.

145
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:01,880
Spirits, be gone!

146
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,480
You know what to do, Skye!

147
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:23,960
Farrow, take this card!

148
00:14:24,660 --> 00:14:25,490
Ironheart!

149
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:29,480
You've disrupted my plans
for the last time, old man.

150
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,520
Ironheart, no!

151
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,230
Grandfather!

152
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:41,940
Please take this card from me.

153
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,060
It's the only way to defeat that beast.

154
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:49,360
I can't get out!

155
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,430
Grandpa!

156
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:52,622
It's up to you.

157
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,351
What do you mean, Gramps?

158
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:59,320
Take this and bring it to the Pharaoh.

159
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,560
Otherwise, all hope is lost.

160
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,030
Good luck.

161
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,120
No, Grandpa!

162
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:12,120
Come on, Skye!

163
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:18,840
Stay back!

164
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:29,420
My guardian's in trouble,
so I'll play Koribo!

165
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,420
Here I come!

166
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,280
Guess again.

167
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:44,260
Chris, are you alright?

168
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,600
Yeah, I think so.

169
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:50,810
No!

170
00:15:51,100 --> 00:15:52,335
Skye's been captured!

171
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:00,840
Please, Chris, turn back!

172
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,413
It's far too dangerous!

173
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:03,690
Sparrow!

174
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:06,640
Grandpa wanted you to have this! No!

175
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:12,960
Chris, no!

176
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:18,560
Pharaoh, take this, please.

177
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,060
What is it?

178
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:24,440
It's the only thing that can stop him.

179
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:28,800
It saved us once, and with your
help, it can save us again.

180
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:31,640
The eye of Tomas.

181
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:34,160
I trust you, Pharaoh.

182
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,000
Thank you.

183
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,320
Hold on!

184
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:39,500
Come back!

185
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:50,220
There's only one thing left to do.

186
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,960
I hope you deem me worthy of your power.

187
00:16:54,400 --> 00:16:57,080
I'm truly sorry for having betrayed you.

188
00:16:57,340 --> 00:17:01,360
But the lives of so many innocent
people are depending on you.

189
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:05,900
So I ask you, not for myself,
but for all those at risk.

190
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,520
Please, help me, Tamaeus.

191
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:12,820
The future of two worlds
hangs in the balance.

192
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:14,320
We must win.

193
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:23,780
Now I sacrifice my Celtic guardian in
order to summon Dark Magician Girl!

194
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:30,640
Next I'll play the
legendary Eye of Tamaeus!

195
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:46,657
He'll never learn I don't believe it He
should never have been able to summon that

196
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:50,757
dragon Dark Magician
Girl Fuse with Timaeus

197
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:54,980
Forming Dark Magician
Girl The Dragon Knight

198
00:17:56,340 --> 00:18:00,760
Next I'll enhance your strength
With my Excalibur Magic Card

199
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:06,360
Attack Mark, destroy his
creature of darkness!

200
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:29,531
This isn't over, Pharaoh.

201
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:35,702
I'm assuming you see that gigantic
green sunset over there, right?

202
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:37,672
What do you think it is?

203
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,864
I'm guessing it's got
something to do with this.

204
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Let's just hope Taya and
the Pharaoh are all right.

205
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:47,820
Hey, wait!

206
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:49,667
It's your turn to carry Rex.

207
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:51,380
I know you can hear me!

208
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,380
Well done, my creatures.

209
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,700
He's gone now, thanks to you two.

210
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,580
But I feel this is just the beginning.

211
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:12,320
I have to say I'm glad you won, Pharaoh.

212
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:17,160
Because now I can be the one who
delivers your soul to Master Darts.

213
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:25,740
Wait, that's a carving of Ironheart,
Chris, and Skye from 10,000 years ago? Yes.

214
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:29,697
So you mean to tell me that those
guys were just ghosts or something?

215
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:32,368
They're spirits who
once fought a great war.

216
00:19:32,780 --> 00:19:35,400
And now they've been captured by darts.

217
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:39,957
This gives me three more
reasons to hunt down this

218
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,860
madman and bring peace
to the world once again.
